<title>BULGARIA: APRIL INDUSTRIAL SALES FALL 17 PCT YR/YR.</title>
<headline>APRIL INDUSTRIAL SALES FALL 17 PCT YR/YR.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Industrial sales of Bulgaria's</p>
<p>state and private sectors in April fell a real 17 percent from</p>
<p>the same month of 1996 to 1,170 billion levs at current prices,</p>
<p>National Statistics Institute (NSI) figures showed.</p>
<p>Sales of the both sectors in the first four months of 1997</p>
<p>totalled 3,842 billion levs at current prices, down a real 18</p>
<p>percent from the same period of last year.</p>
<p> RECEIPTS FROM IND. SALES	  APRIL	JAN-APRIL</p>
<p> yr/yr change, pct real	    -17.0	  -18.0</p>
<p> billion BGL, current prices     1,170	  3,842</p>
<p>RECEIPTS FROM IND. SALES</p>
<p>(STATE SECTOR)</p>
<p> yr/yr change, pct real	    -19.0	  -19.2</p>
<p> billion BGL, current prices	 956	  3,150</p>
<p>RECEIPTS FROM IND. SALES</p>
<p>(PRIVATE SECTOR)</p>
<p> yr/yr change, pct real	    -10.0	   -7.0</p>
<p> billion BGL, current prices	 214	    692</p>
<p>Domestic sales from both sectors fell a real 32 percent</p>
<p>year on year in April and a real 30 percent in the first four</p>
<p>months.</p>
<p>Exports by both sectors rose a real 6.8 percent year on</p>
<p>year in April and a real 1.9 percent from January through April</p>
<p>compared to the same period last year.</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-91188</p>
</text>
